No docs. Create the module.

Note import in test: "../apps/client/src/lib/projects/terminal-title.ts" with .ts extension — Bun resolves fine.

Write file with Korean doc comments consistent with repo style.

Implementation details:

```ts
export type Harness = "pi" | "claude" | string; // accept string
```

Test calls taskTitle("claude", ...) so signature (harness: string, title: string | null | undefined).

Code:

```ts
/** 스피너 글리프. pi 의 titlebar-spinner 확장은 점자 프레임을, Claude Code 는 ✳·✻·· 를 제목 앞에 붙인다. */
const SPINNER = /^[\u2800-\u28ff\u00b7\u2022\u2217*\u2733\u2736\u2739\u273b\u273d\u273f\u2740\u2742]+\s*/u;

/** Claude Code 가 아무 작업도 하지 않을 때 두는 기본 제목. */
const CLAUDE_IDLE = new Set(["Claude Code", "Claude"]);

export function taskTitle(harness: string, title: string | null | undefined): string | null {
	const text = (title ?? "").replace(SPINNER, "").trim();
	if (!text) return null;
	if (harness === "claude") return CLAUDE_IDLE.has(text) ? null : text;
	return piSession(text);
}

function piSession(title: string): string | null {
	const parts = title.split(" - ");
	if (parts.length < 3) return null;
	const name = parts.slice(1, -1).join(" - ").trim();
	return name || null;
}
```

Wait: claude title "✳ Claude Code" after strip → "Claude Code" → null. Good. What if claude title is "Claude Code" plus something? fine.

But should claude also handle generic titles like "✳" only → null. Yes after strip empty.

pi title "π - fix login - dashboard" → parts ['π','fix login','dashboard'] → 'fix login'. Good. "Pi-Bolt - a - b - dashboard" → 'a - b'. Good. "π - dashboard" → 2 parts → null. Good.

Also possible pi title "π - fix login - dashboard - ..." no.

Edge: pi title without app prefix but with session: e.g. "fix login - dashboard". Would return null incorrectly, but format always app-prefixed. Could additionally handle by basename compare? Not available. Keep.

Hmm, but maybe an issue: pi titles can have spinner without space: "⠋π - fix - dashboard" — regex handles.

Also, claude could have the title include cwd? Claude Code sets title as `✳ <title>`? Fine.

Add a `piAppTitle` check? Could verify first segment: but custom APP_NAME allowed. Accept any.

Actually, should we guard against first segment containing " - " from a session-less title? Not needed.

Write the file, run test. Also maybe run typecheck/lint on that file? Let's write then run bun test and maybe bunx tsc check via package check (could be slow). I'll at least run prettier/biome lint if configured.

